WEBVTT

00:00:30.810 --> 00:00:33.890
<i> A strange old man lives here.</i>

00:00:44.960 --> 00:00:47.470
<i> On a piece of paper the size of 120 tatami mats</i>

00:00:47.470 --> 00:00:50.050
<i> he painted a large portrait of Bodhidharma.</i>

00:00:50.560 --> 00:00:52.240
<i> But that's not all...</i>

00:00:52.680 --> 00:00:56.080
<i> Then he painted two sparrows
on one grain of rice.</i>

00:01:01.660 --> 00:01:03.480
<i> If you don't already know Tetsuzo,</i>

00:01:03.480 --> 00:01:07.080
<i> you probably heard about the artist called Hokusai.</i>

00:01:08.650 --> 00:01:12.200
<i> And this strange old man... Is my father.</i>

00:01:52.440 --> 00:01:54.440
A heap of dog shit...

00:01:54.820 --> 00:01:57.970
Bubble. Bubble!

00:02:12.160 --> 00:02:16.670
Summer '11 Bunka era (1814). Edo City.

00:02:25.640 --> 00:02:26.610
Who's there?

00:02:26.610 --> 00:02:27.720
It's me!

00:02:27.720 --> 00:02:30.440
Ah, Oei.

00:02:30.440 --> 00:02:32.760
I brought lunch.

00:02:32.760 --> 00:02:34.000
Thank you!

00:02:44.040 --> 00:02:47.450
I heard your dad is taking fewer jobs?

00:02:49.390 --> 00:02:50.600
Who said that?

00:02:51.530 --> 00:02:53.510
Oh... rumors.

00:02:53.510 --> 00:02:56.520
I hope he eats well.

00:02:56.520 --> 00:02:58.640
What is he going to do if he doesn't eat?

00:02:58.640 --> 00:03:02.080
We're father and daughter, with 2 brushes
and 2 pairs of chopsticks,

00:03:02.080 --> 00:03:05.230
we can always manage somehow.

00:03:09.840 --> 00:03:13.500
Oh yes...
I recently went to see Onao.

00:03:13.500 --> 00:03:16.170
She took her new yukata

00:03:16.170 --> 00:03:18.830
and told me it has been a while since you visited,

00:03:18.830 --> 00:03:21.680
and that she wants you
to buy her a goldfish.

00:03:23.260 --> 00:03:24.360
Yeah.

00:03:24.940 --> 00:03:28.190
A goldfish that she
can look at every day.

00:03:31.230 --> 00:03:35.010
She'll look at it even
when she can't see.

00:03:38.670 --> 00:03:40.200
She can see.

00:03:54.830 --> 00:03:58.930
Mama,
can I come live with you?

00:03:58.930 --> 00:04:01.100
I would be really happy,

00:04:01.100 --> 00:04:03.770
but what about your dad?

00:04:03.770 --> 00:04:08.370
Even if Tetsuzo was alone and split in half, he could handle himself.

00:04:08.370 --> 00:04:11.740
Do not talk about your dad as
if he were a lizard.

00:04:15.760 --> 00:04:17.720
Sarusuberi finally blossomed.

00:04:18.350 --> 00:04:23.160
<i> Senseless bloom,
only then to colorfully crumble.</i>

00:04:23.160 --> 00:04:26.690
The long celebrations have begun...

00:04:29.080 --> 00:04:35.880
Sarusuberi: Miss Hokusai

00:04:58.350 --> 00:05:02.460
<i> This is the house where I live with Tetsuzo.</i>

00:05:02.460 --> 00:05:05.880
<i> There's no organization
and nothing is cleaned.</i>

00:05:05.880 --> 00:05:08.820
<i> When the trash becomes
too much, we just move it.</i>

00:05:08.820 --> 00:05:11.990
<i> Tetsuzo is not interested in anything
besides painting.</i>

00:05:11.990 --> 00:05:14.040
<i> He does not drink or smoke.</i>

00:05:14.810 --> 00:05:19.370
<i> Although... Judging by his erotic drawings,
he certainly likes women.</i>

00:05:39.060 --> 00:05:41.670
[painting's author - Hokusai]

00:05:50.170 --> 00:05:52.760
He drew it and then destroyed it?!

00:05:53.230 --> 00:05:54.860
I don't understand!

00:05:54.860 --> 00:05:57.020
Let me see Sensei!

00:05:57.740 --> 00:05:59.630
Well, who knows where he is...

00:05:59.630 --> 00:06:01.500
Don't play with me!

00:06:02.400 --> 00:06:03.840
He isn't here...

00:06:06.680 --> 00:06:08.160
He really isn't there.

00:06:08.160 --> 00:06:10.440
Sensei! Where's the dragon drawing?!

00:06:10.440 --> 00:06:13.870
As soon as I finished it,
he immediately soared into the sky.

00:06:14.760 --> 00:06:18.010
What are you worried about?
We agreed at the end of the month.

00:06:18.010 --> 00:06:20.760
There's another day until the end of the month.

00:06:20.760 --> 00:06:22.780
Come back tomorrow.

00:06:22.780 --> 00:06:25.370
Maybe he will have come back from the heavens by then.

00:06:25.920 --> 00:06:28.510
And if he doesn't return?

00:06:28.510 --> 00:06:30.110
Do as you wish.

00:06:34.770 --> 00:06:39.280
Even if I cut off your head,
my lord will not be satisfied.

00:06:39.280 --> 00:06:41.410
I have no choice...

00:06:41.980 --> 00:06:44.140
Would cutting your belly hurt?

00:06:46.030 --> 00:06:47.880
It must hurt...

00:06:57.880 --> 00:07:00.490
I won't have it ready by tomorrow.

00:07:00.490 --> 00:07:02.000
I know.

00:07:04.910 --> 00:07:07.760
I think we shouldn't do it after all, brother.

00:07:09.020 --> 00:07:11.000
What are you saying?

00:07:11.000 --> 00:07:14.760
Didn't you tell me you wanted to see Hokusai-sensei?

00:07:14.760 --> 00:07:16.960
<i> That drunkard's name is Zenjirou.</i>

00:07:16.960 --> 00:07:20.680
<i> This parasite lives with us
and is a shameless womanizer.</i>

00:07:20.680 --> 00:07:22.270
<i> He used to be a samurai,</i>

00:07:22.270 --> 00:07:26.000
<i> but then, for some reason, decided
to put down the katana and took up the brush.</i>

00:07:31.160 --> 00:07:34.370
I met this guy at the printer.

00:07:35.040 --> 00:07:36.410
Hey, rookie!

00:07:36.410 --> 00:07:40.170
When you become an artist,
you'll have me to thank!

00:07:40.170 --> 00:07:43.730
This old man here – he's the celebrated Hokusai.

00:07:43.730 --> 00:07:45.820
This is a great honor for me!

00:07:45.820 --> 00:07:50.440
I am a student of Utagawa Toyokuni.
My name is Utagawa Kuninao.

00:07:50.440 --> 00:07:54.470
Eventhough I am a follower of the Utagawa school,
I have great respect for you, Hokusai-sensei!

00:07:54.470 --> 00:07:57.930
Thank you for taking your time to see me!

00:08:00.720 --> 00:08:02.480
Kuninao?

00:08:02.480 --> 00:08:04.820
Why didn't you tell me this before?!

00:08:04.820 --> 00:08:06.890
You didn't ask me.

00:08:06.890 --> 00:08:10.510
I see, you're Kuninao...

00:08:10.510 --> 00:08:12.260
You're pretty popular.

00:08:12.260 --> 00:08:14.520
No no, you exaggerate!

00:08:15.200 --> 00:08:16.330
Come on!

00:08:16.330 --> 00:08:17.520
Yes.

00:08:19.400 --> 00:08:21.050
So, you're only 19 years old?

00:08:21.050 --> 00:08:22.030
Yes.

00:08:22.430 --> 00:08:25.550
You're younger than me for 4 years...

00:08:26.890 --> 00:08:28.040
Eat!

00:08:28.040 --> 00:08:28.900
No, I...

00:08:28.900 --> 00:08:32.360
Come eat up, lanky!

00:08:34.650 --> 00:08:37.070
Please stop it brother!

00:08:38.060 --> 00:08:41.180
Forgive us for the trouble.

00:08:42.220 --> 00:08:44.530
Oh! Dog shit...

00:08:44.530 --> 00:08:45.660
Oh!

00:08:48.600 --> 00:08:50.500
Hmm... Do you know her?

00:08:50.500 --> 00:08:52.980
This is Sensei's daughter, Oei.

00:08:52.980 --> 00:08:55.340
So the lady's name is Oei-san?

00:08:55.340 --> 00:08:59.610
I see how it is...
I often see her at Ryogoku Bridge.

00:09:07.840 --> 00:09:10.330
Dragon, huh?

00:09:10.330 --> 00:09:12.520
The dragon has a secret:

00:09:13.290 --> 00:09:15.850
you need to paint with the tip of the brush.

00:09:15.850 --> 00:09:18.110
Visualize it in your head,

00:09:18.110 --> 00:09:20.410
then wait until it has come down,

00:09:20.410 --> 00:09:23.050
as if the dragon came to life.

00:09:24.330 --> 00:09:25.850
And after he comes into this world,

00:09:25.850 --> 00:09:28.240
sketch it rapidly with small strokes of the brush.

00:09:28.240 --> 00:09:30.860
This creature is different from all the others.

00:09:30.860 --> 00:09:32.910
So the way it's portrayed is also very different.

00:09:33.520 --> 00:09:36.950
Ah, that's not my idea.

00:09:36.950 --> 00:09:39.040
I was told that story.

00:09:41.610 --> 00:09:43.440
Stop!

00:09:43.440 --> 00:09:46.590
Flirting with Oei-chan in front of her father...

00:09:46.590 --> 00:09:48.270
You got some nerve!

00:09:48.690 --> 00:09:50.530
No... Not at all!

00:09:50.530 --> 00:09:52.190
That's not what I...

00:09:52.190 --> 00:09:54.000
As expected of the more popular artists.

00:09:54.000 --> 00:09:56.030
Girls love clever guys.

00:09:57.730 --> 00:09:58.970
Oh, you bastard!

00:10:00.090 --> 00:10:01.500
Stop trying to show off!

00:10:01.500 --> 00:10:02.590
Hey!

00:10:06.720 --> 00:10:07.450
Yes?

00:10:10.170 --> 00:10:12.170
Get out of here!

00:10:17.850 --> 00:10:20.760
What's this...
She even put her old man.

00:10:22.160 --> 00:10:24.810
Sensei!
Should we take a walk?

00:10:24.810 --> 00:10:25.790
Alright.

00:10:25.790 --> 00:10:27.920
Maybe have a drink?

00:10:47.100 --> 00:10:50.940
Look at the fox.
She's trying to lure us.

00:10:51.440 --> 00:10:53.540
Ah... She laughed.

00:10:54.840 --> 00:10:57.550
No dragons there!

00:10:58.520 --> 00:11:01.490
I saw one in the province of Shinshu,
when I was a kid.

00:11:01.490 --> 00:11:03.310
It was probably just a whirlwind.

00:11:03.310 --> 00:11:08.440
When the wind drops from the mountains and into the valley,
it forms a vortex of swirling sand.

00:11:08.440 --> 00:11:09.670
I also saw them.

00:11:11.390 --> 00:11:14.680
I clearly saw
his claws in the midst of the clouds.

00:11:15.320 --> 00:11:17.180
That was just your imagination.

00:11:17.660 --> 00:11:21.200
You are so limited.
That's why you draw badly.

00:11:21.200 --> 00:11:21.950
Eh?

00:11:22.430 --> 00:11:25.120
People just look terrible on your paintings.

00:11:25.560 --> 00:11:31.880
It feels that if they took just one step,
they'd immediately drain into a puddle of mud.

00:11:37.130 --> 00:11:40.120
Nevertheless,
your paintings have an interesting smell.

00:11:40.690 --> 00:11:43.610
And when a lot of them accumulate,
the room starts getting stuffy.

00:11:46.460 --> 00:11:49.140
And you have talent,
so beware of the hatred.

00:11:50.180 --> 00:11:52.040
Hatred?!

00:11:52.040 --> 00:11:55.440
Yes, exactly. It is very dangerous.

00:11:55.440 --> 00:11:59.230
Beware of envious glances
from other students.

00:11:59.230 --> 00:12:00.200
Yes.

00:12:00.810 --> 00:12:01.990
Hey, you...

00:12:01.990 --> 00:12:04.830
I completely stopped understanding,
what you are talking about.

00:12:04.940 --> 00:12:06.090
What?!

00:12:06.090 --> 00:12:09.630
You should not interfere
in our conversations, fox! I am ashamed!

00:12:09.630 --> 00:12:12.120
Oh, it looks like you're angry.

00:12:12.120 --> 00:12:14.450
You don't understand, woman!

00:12:14.450 --> 00:12:17.210
This old man – Hokusai-sensei!

00:12:17.210 --> 00:12:17.890
Hmm?

00:12:22.640 --> 00:12:24.670
You're lying!

00:12:28.240 --> 00:12:29.630
Of course!

00:12:31.480 --> 00:12:32.750
Oh, you pranksters!

00:13:37.600 --> 00:13:41.820
You are the only one left.
The rest have gone before dawn.

00:13:44.260 --> 00:13:47.170
They threw me out, the bastards...

00:13:52.760 --> 00:13:55.270
Shoo! Shoo!

00:13:59.900 --> 00:14:01.150
Hmm?

00:14:41.200 --> 00:14:42.360
What do you want?

00:14:57.300 --> 00:15:00.700
You must be very curious
to come to this house.

00:15:01.480 --> 00:15:04.200
Heh! We're pretty similar.

00:15:47.210 --> 00:15:48.080
Onao!

00:15:49.760 --> 00:15:50.670
Nee-chan!

00:15:52.770 --> 00:15:55.180
The Mother Superior gave me permission,

00:15:55.180 --> 00:15:57.010
so wanna take a walk outside?

00:15:58.490 --> 00:16:01.480
<i> Onao is blind from birth.</i>

00:16:02.170 --> 00:16:05.590
Oei-san, you have paint on your face.

00:16:07.980 --> 00:16:09.280
Did you clean it?

00:16:10.980 --> 00:16:11.870
Yeah.

00:16:12.840 --> 00:16:14.040
Where do you want to go?

00:16:14.040 --> 00:16:15.050
The bridge.

00:16:15.470 --> 00:16:16.680
The bridge again?

00:16:16.680 --> 00:16:19.110
You sure love the bridge, Onao.

00:16:24.320 --> 00:16:28.310
Pepper Ton-Ton!
Spicy hot pepper!

00:16:33.310 --> 00:16:36.190
Honeyed rice balls!

00:16:51.050 --> 00:16:53.280
You can listen to a lot of different voices.

00:16:53.280 --> 00:16:54.560
And smells, too.

00:16:54.560 --> 00:16:56.970
Yes. It is very interesting.

00:16:56.970 --> 00:16:59.310
I love this bridge too.

00:17:06.970 --> 00:17:08.200
Rice crackers?

00:17:08.200 --> 00:17:09.760
Ishiwara rice crackers?

00:17:09.760 --> 00:17:12.700
No, Tozaki. Try it.

00:17:22.930 --> 00:17:26.450
Dad never comes to see me.

00:17:26.450 --> 00:17:27.700
I wonder why.

00:17:27.700 --> 00:17:30.030
He's very busy working, that's all.

00:17:30.030 --> 00:17:33.520
It's not like he hates you.

00:17:33.520 --> 00:17:38.750
With such a weak body, I'll never
be able to properly honor dad and mom,

00:17:38.750 --> 00:17:41.800
so when I die, I'll probably go to hell.

00:17:41.800 --> 00:17:43.580
That's not true!

00:17:48.580 --> 00:17:52.080
<i> Tetsuzo is a coward, and a crybaby!</i>

00:17:54.810 --> 00:17:55.820
Oei-san?

00:17:59.520 --> 00:18:01.290
So this is Sensei's youngest daughter?

00:18:01.290 --> 00:18:02.400
Her name is Onao.

00:18:02.400 --> 00:18:05.340
She lives in a monastery and is learning to play the biwa.

00:18:05.340 --> 00:18:07.950
I heard from Sensei.

00:18:08.770 --> 00:18:12.440
Onao-san,
I am a student of your father – Hatsugoro.

00:18:12.440 --> 00:18:15.630
My artistic pseudonym is Totoya Hokkei.

00:18:16.320 --> 00:18:18.690
Totoya? Fishmonger?

00:18:16.900 --> 00:18:18.690
TL: The characters for 'Toto-ya' (魚屋) can be read as 'Sakana-ya' which means fishmonger.

00:18:18.690 --> 00:18:21.850
Yes.
Before, I used to sell fish.

00:18:24.580 --> 00:18:25.890
What are you doing here?

00:18:25.890 --> 00:18:29.930
We just came to see the bridge,
listen to the voices, the smell, that's all.

00:18:30.610 --> 00:18:33.620
It's great.
The bridge is a very interesting place.

00:18:35.210 --> 00:18:36.420
By the way...

00:18:38.800 --> 00:18:42.080
Your recent bijin-ga was very good!

00:18:42.080 --> 00:18:44.760
Much better than mine.

00:18:44.760 --> 00:18:47.160
That's not... true.

00:18:47.160 --> 00:18:49.850
No no.
I really meant that.

00:18:59.020 --> 00:19:02.250
Now, excuse me,
I need to go to the printer.

00:19:02.250 --> 00:19:04.500
Goodbye, Onao-san!

00:19:16.270 --> 00:19:18.700
Oei-san, take this.

00:19:21.060 --> 00:19:21.960
Here.

00:19:23.460 --> 00:19:24.640
Clean it better.

00:19:24.640 --> 00:19:26.350
You have such a pretty face after all.

00:19:26.350 --> 00:19:27.360
Bye.

00:19:39.550 --> 00:19:42.250
He's a kind man, isn't he?

00:19:42.250 --> 00:19:44.300
Yes, very kind.

00:19:44.300 --> 00:19:46.680
And you were not the same as usual, Nee-chan.

00:19:46.680 --> 00:19:49.340
That's not... true.

00:19:54.010 --> 00:19:55.790
I know, let's take a boat ride!

00:20:03.530 --> 00:20:06.200
Well?
Feels nice, right?

00:20:08.480 --> 00:20:11.480
We're sailing under the bridge now.

00:20:32.890 --> 00:20:34.140
Scared?

00:20:43.620 --> 00:20:46.400
If we keep going, where will we end up?

00:20:46.400 --> 00:20:47.340
The sea.

00:20:47.800 --> 00:20:49.530
The sea is very big.

00:20:49.530 --> 00:20:52.820
Much bigger than Honjo and Asakusa.
Much more!

00:20:52.820 --> 00:20:54.060
Eh?

00:20:54.060 --> 00:20:56.150
Tetsuzo often draws the sea.

00:20:56.150 --> 00:20:58.270
The waves can be very scary.

00:20:58.270 --> 00:21:01.370
A huge wave could easily sink a boat.

00:21:01.370 --> 00:21:02.670
Waves?

00:21:52.830 --> 00:21:54.200
Oh oh oh!

00:22:02.040 --> 00:22:04.820
Give me a break, Sensei.

00:22:08.100 --> 00:22:11.240
You need to be able to draw vile things as well

00:22:11.240 --> 00:22:14.250
You're really cruel.

00:22:16.470 --> 00:22:18.920
Look, your face is dirty.

00:22:20.110 --> 00:22:21.380
What's this?

00:22:22.220 --> 00:22:24.350
Well... It's a sketch.

00:22:25.170 --> 00:22:27.260
Neck pattern copied from Eizan,

00:22:27.260 --> 00:22:31.050
and the composition is clearly borrowed
from Utamaro, isn't it?

00:22:31.050 --> 00:22:31.890
Well...

00:22:32.790 --> 00:22:34.320
You're right...

00:22:35.080 --> 00:22:37.780
This is why Oei
calls you "dumb Zen."

00:22:40.100 --> 00:22:43.970
Well, Oei-chan's art is much better.

00:22:43.970 --> 00:22:45.700
I can't compete.

00:22:46.890 --> 00:22:49.260
That's where you're wrong.

00:22:49.260 --> 00:22:50.370
Eh?

00:22:50.370 --> 00:22:52.190
She's good at drawing women,

00:22:52.190 --> 00:22:54.680
sometimes I even think she's better than me,

00:22:54.680 --> 00:22:59.690
but when it comes to men, she can only imitate my drawings.

00:23:01.020 --> 00:23:01.950
Eh...

00:23:02.430 --> 00:23:06.500
That idiot betrays painting by isolating that one topic.

00:23:07.890 --> 00:23:10.230
Something Oei-chan can't do...

00:23:10.230 --> 00:23:13.360
I'm telling you, the important thing is to not put your hands down.

00:23:13.360 --> 00:23:17.680
Forcing his own daughter to draw this... That's very mean of you, Sensei.

00:23:17.680 --> 00:23:20.000
She thinks
she can draw anything,

00:23:20.000 --> 00:23:22.390
and refuses to back down,
even if the painting doesn't come out.

00:23:29.950 --> 00:23:31.010
Welcome back.

00:23:31.920 --> 00:23:33.480
What do you want, Zen?

00:23:34.140 --> 00:23:35.170
Nothing.

00:23:49.170 --> 00:23:50.490
You're leaving again?

00:23:50.900 --> 00:23:53.950
Yes, I'm going to Yoshiwara
to paint a portrait of a courtesan.

00:23:54.270 --> 00:23:55.900
What?

00:23:56.920 --> 00:24:00.690
Manjidou said he wanted it in color.

00:24:01.150 --> 00:24:04.180
Hmm... What's her name? And where she works?

00:24:05.010 --> 00:24:06.390
And why do you ask?

00:24:06.740 --> 00:24:08.660
Ah... Nothing.

00:24:14.100 --> 00:24:15.940
It's Sayogoromo at Kikyo-ya.

00:24:15.940 --> 00:24:16.610
Uh?!

00:24:17.960 --> 00:24:19.940
What? Do you know her?

00:24:29.420 --> 00:24:32.320
About this courtesan Sayogoromo, recently

00:24:32.320 --> 00:24:34.500
there's been a lot of rumors about her.

00:24:34.500 --> 00:24:37.060
Rumors? Like?

00:24:41.410 --> 00:24:43.460
[One woman]

00:24:44.280 --> 00:24:46.440
It is said that at dawn

00:24:46.440 --> 00:24:49.540
the head of the courtesan is separated from the body.

00:24:49.540 --> 00:24:51.450
Separated from the body?

00:24:51.450 --> 00:24:54.510
The client appeared very scared

00:24:54.510 --> 00:24:56.880
but no one else saw anything...

00:24:57.460 --> 00:24:59.680
Well, maybe it was all a dream.

00:24:59.680 --> 00:25:03.380
This Sayogoromo always seems very mysterious. They say that when she sleep

00:25:03.380 --> 00:25:07.580
her head slips away from the pillow until it's morning.

00:25:07.580 --> 00:25:09.380
You sure you saw that?

00:25:09.380 --> 00:25:10.980
I saw it with my own eyes!

00:25:10.980 --> 00:25:13.120
This means that her neck
somehow extends.

00:25:13.120 --> 00:25:14.450
What?!

00:25:14.450 --> 00:25:19.730
Like someone as narrow-minded as you is going to see a ghost.

00:25:37.820 --> 00:25:40.000
Oei-san,
your drawings are beautiful.

00:25:40.550 --> 00:25:42.860
I look better than I actually do in them.

00:25:44.780 --> 00:25:47.550
You really have a talent for drawing.

00:25:48.410 --> 00:25:51.390
This is the outline I will use to
draw the final painting.

00:25:52.050 --> 00:25:54.100
And then we'll turn it into a nishiki-e.

00:25:55.400 --> 00:25:57.310
I can not wait to see them.

00:26:00.040 --> 00:26:01.780
Sorry to keep you waiting.

00:26:01.780 --> 00:26:04.320
So, what's your business here?

00:26:11.990 --> 00:26:16.410
If you want to be entertained,
go to East Ryogoku.

00:26:16.880 --> 00:26:19.730
Here in Yoshiwara we do not play around!

00:26:20.530 --> 00:26:21.980
Forgive me, lady!

00:26:22.480 --> 00:26:23.610
Let go!

00:26:23.610 --> 00:26:26.510
This old man really needs to talk with you!

00:26:26.510 --> 00:26:28.730
Please at least listen to him!

00:26:30.830 --> 00:26:34.350
I will not take much of your time.
Have a sit.

00:26:43.230 --> 00:26:46.690
I'm her father and also an artist.

00:26:47.280 --> 00:26:50.900
Let's see... This story took place before her birth.

00:26:50.900 --> 00:26:53.140
So about 25 years ago.

00:26:54.570 --> 00:26:57.070
I was ordered
to paint a painting of monsters.

00:26:57.920 --> 00:26:59.950
I drew it until it got dark,

00:26:59.950 --> 00:27:01.600
and then decided to take a nap.

00:27:01.600 --> 00:27:04.750
And suddenly I heard "tuk-tuk, tuk-tuk."
Something was hitting the tatami.

00:27:05.450 --> 00:27:07.680
It was my own hands.

00:27:07.680 --> 00:27:10.340
They crazily danced by themselves.

00:27:10.340 --> 00:27:13.360
And then, out of my hands,

00:27:13.360 --> 00:27:16.380
something came out and flew out the window.

00:27:16.380 --> 00:27:17.920
Only hands flew out.

00:27:17.920 --> 00:27:19.640
And it was dark, so I couldn't see more.

00:27:19.640 --> 00:27:23.550
I could feel the wind in my fingers, it was extremely cold,

00:27:23.550 --> 00:27:26.360
that's how I realized they were extremely fast.

00:27:26.650 --> 00:27:29.370
And after that I felt it every night.

00:27:30.980 --> 00:27:32.810
It scared me at first.

00:27:32.810 --> 00:27:34.960
But then I got used to it
and found it quite interesting.

00:27:40.830 --> 00:27:43.170
Sometimes they'd rip up the miscanthus fields.

00:27:45.670 --> 00:27:48.490
Sometimes wrap around the spire of the five-story pagoda.

00:27:49.260 --> 00:27:51.450
Sometimes they swept under the bridge.

00:27:51.990 --> 00:27:53.300
One day I thought:

00:27:53.300 --> 00:27:57.280
"If these flying hands were cut off somewhere,

00:27:57.280 --> 00:27:59.920
could I use my real hands that are left behind?"

00:28:00.800 --> 00:28:02.850
After all, I have yet to draw enough.

00:28:02.850 --> 00:28:04.770
When I told a friend monk,

00:28:04.770 --> 00:28:06.820
they told me I shouldn't do it.

00:28:08.170 --> 00:28:12.080
So he scribbled sutras in my hands
and wrapped them in rosary prayer.

00:28:13.380 --> 00:28:16.350
Since then, it never happened again.

00:28:16.350 --> 00:28:20.410
And as you can see, I turned into a fine artist.
End of story.

00:28:21.200 --> 00:28:23.410
Congratulations.

00:28:29.460 --> 00:28:32.740
When you hear the sound of the bell,
go to the next room.

00:28:34.050 --> 00:28:38.510
And if you will not hear anything until the morning, please, return home.

00:28:40.620 --> 00:28:42.050
This stays between us.

00:28:42.050 --> 00:28:43.320
Do you agree?

00:29:15.920 --> 00:29:18.640
Everything is as usual...

00:29:18.640 --> 00:29:21.840
You didn't need to stay with us.

00:29:21.840 --> 00:29:23.150
Do what you want.

00:29:25.180 --> 00:29:28.050
Well, from time to time this is nice too.

00:29:41.370 --> 00:29:42.410
Shut up already.

00:29:43.370 --> 00:29:44.400
Eh?

00:29:44.400 --> 00:29:46.320
I didn't say anything.

00:29:47.150 --> 00:29:50.110
You have been sighing all this time.

00:29:53.590 --> 00:29:56.540
Well, after such a long night...

00:29:59.010 --> 00:30:00.500
Crickets?

00:30:52.400 --> 00:30:54.110
Do see something?

00:30:54.550 --> 00:30:55.580
Eh?

00:31:06.240 --> 00:31:06.940
Shut up!

00:31:14.620 --> 00:31:16.700
It can't get out of the mosquito net.

00:31:16.700 --> 00:31:18.830
It's like a barrier.

00:31:38.290 --> 00:31:40.450
Good thing the net was here.

00:31:41.010 --> 00:31:43.810
It could have flown over it at any time.

00:31:43.810 --> 00:31:45.610
But if you do that...

00:31:46.640 --> 00:31:50.750
What would you suggest? For me to fill my neck with sutras and wrap it in rosary?

00:31:51.480 --> 00:31:53.840
And if your head doesn't come back, then what?

00:31:54.380 --> 00:31:57.690
We'll see when the time comes.

00:32:02.430 --> 00:32:07.040
Who would have thought it'd really come out...

00:32:09.550 --> 00:32:13.290
By the way, Sensei,
that's the first time I hear that story.

00:32:13.290 --> 00:32:15.070
About the flying hands.

00:32:15.070 --> 00:32:18.000
Don't be an idiot.
It's the first time I told it too.

00:32:18.000 --> 00:32:18.990
Eh?

00:32:18.990 --> 00:32:22.790
This is an old story,
written by Bakin.

00:32:22.790 --> 00:32:24.560
Why do you do it then?

00:32:26.700 --> 00:32:30.920
If I hadn't told her, we wouldn't have been able to see such a wonderful show.

00:32:30.920 --> 00:32:33.550
I don't understand it.

00:32:33.550 --> 00:32:36.800
I would prefer to look at something else.

00:32:36.800 --> 00:32:39.950
That's why some of your drawings are so bad...

00:33:23.630 --> 00:33:26.220
<i> I just couldn't pass this up!</i>

00:33:26.220 --> 00:33:30.120
<i> As soon as I heard the sound of the bells,
I immediately tried to get closer.</i>

00:33:30.570 --> 00:33:31.850
Stop messing around!

00:33:34.140 --> 00:33:35.850
The fire is spreading!

00:33:49.550 --> 00:33:52.270
Pull! Pull!

00:34:04.410 --> 00:34:05.790
Hey, you! Bring it back!

00:34:05.790 --> 00:34:07.470
Hurry up!

00:34:07.930 --> 00:34:10.510
Look at it fall!

00:34:15.000 --> 00:34:16.990
<i> Watching firefighters fight with the burning house,</i>

00:34:16.990 --> 00:34:19.280
<i> watching a fireball ikebana
blossoms in the sky, seeing it die,</i>

00:34:19.280 --> 00:34:22.580
<i> it is such an indescribable feeling
that I'm simply lost for words...</i>

00:34:42.450 --> 00:34:43.810
Another fire?

00:34:46.240 --> 00:34:48.510
Why do you like them so much?

00:35:01.740 --> 00:35:06.350
This is the same as what you have for women, and Tetsuzo for sweets.

00:35:10.740 --> 00:35:12.140
I see.

00:35:14.080 --> 00:35:15.730
Heh! Idiots...

00:35:57.980 --> 00:36:01.900
The field to your right
is completely covered with snow.

00:36:01.900 --> 00:36:04.130
On this path along the river Okawa,

00:36:04.130 --> 00:36:07.150
it'll take until Spring for the sakura to bloom

00:36:07.150 --> 00:36:11.820
but their bare branches,
covered with snow, also look nice.

00:36:14.650 --> 00:36:16.000
Are you cold?

00:36:26.240 --> 00:36:30.290
[Sanctuary Mimeguri]

00:36:34.140 --> 00:36:36.650
In front of us is the gate to the Mimeguri Inari shrine.

00:36:36.940 --> 00:36:38.960
Since the dam was built here,

00:36:38.960 --> 00:36:41.950
its tip is now directly at your eyes.

00:36:42.800 --> 00:36:46.110
Gates have this form...

00:36:50.040 --> 00:36:52.120
We're going down the stairs now.

00:37:12.580 --> 00:37:14.100
Wait a second.

00:37:14.660 --> 00:37:15.660
What is it?

00:37:16.690 --> 00:37:18.000
Camellia.

00:37:19.740 --> 00:37:22.250
This is my favorite flower.

00:37:23.960 --> 00:37:25.310
Give me your hand.

00:37:30.210 --> 00:37:31.450
And what color is it?

00:37:31.450 --> 00:37:32.670
Red.

00:37:32.670 --> 00:37:35.880
It's gentle and warm color.

00:37:39.080 --> 00:37:40.940
You can take it home.

00:37:40.940 --> 00:37:42.250
I'll put it in your sleeve.

00:38:04.620 --> 00:38:06.130
There is no sound at all.

00:38:07.560 --> 00:38:10.010
Yeah. Complete silence.

00:38:10.010 --> 00:38:12.780
The snow absorbs all the noise.

00:38:14.170 --> 00:38:15.080
Scared?

00:38:22.540 --> 00:38:23.860
It got a bit colder.

00:38:26.400 --> 00:38:27.980
We'd like two amazake!

00:38:30.600 --> 00:38:32.290
I'll go get our order.

00:38:37.030 --> 00:38:38.160
Excuse me...

00:38:39.490 --> 00:38:41.530
Amazake, two of them.

00:38:42.200 --> 00:38:43.320
Yes.

00:40:00.320 --> 00:40:02.990
Throw it up.
As hard as you can.

00:40:24.730 --> 00:40:26.650
Here! Here!

00:40:26.650 --> 00:40:28.210
I'm here! I'm here!

00:40:28.840 --> 00:40:29.820
Take this!

00:40:32.010 --> 00:40:34.330
Take this! And this!

00:40:59.920 --> 00:41:01.680
Here! Here!

00:42:18.160 --> 00:42:19.200
Onao!

00:42:26.560 --> 00:42:30.000
Sorry.
I'm sorry, Nee-chan.

00:42:30.000 --> 00:42:31.230
It's fine.

00:42:31.230 --> 00:42:32.810
You're just a little tired.

00:42:32.810 --> 00:42:34.620
I should have paid more attention.

00:42:34.620 --> 00:42:37.360
But still, today was a lot of fun!

00:42:37.360 --> 00:42:39.550
Snow is so interesting.

00:42:56.750 --> 00:42:59.800
Want to come to my house?
We are very close.

00:43:00.590 --> 00:43:03.020
Dad could be there too.

00:43:03.640 --> 00:43:05.000
Hmmm...

00:43:06.100 --> 00:43:07.340
What do you say?

00:43:07.930 --> 00:43:09.690
If I visited now

00:43:09.690 --> 00:43:11.790
dad would probably be troubled.

00:43:13.050 --> 00:43:16.080
And if dad is troubled, then I'd be too.

00:43:23.040 --> 00:43:24.620
Should we go back then?

00:43:24.620 --> 00:43:25.950
Yeah.

00:44:16.770 --> 00:44:19.790
Madam!
Are you okay?!

00:44:26.670 --> 00:44:29.870
This pattern in the back room...

00:44:29.870 --> 00:44:32.800
I heard the cries of the dead from there!

00:44:36.550 --> 00:44:39.090
We tried to tell her it was the sound of blackbirds in the garden

00:44:39.090 --> 00:44:41.130
but the Madam wouldn't believe us.

00:44:44.770 --> 00:44:45.970
This painting of hell...

00:44:45.970 --> 00:44:48.910
The owner of the house asked Oei-san
to draw him this painting,

00:44:48.910 --> 00:44:52.890
so they could see it every day,
as a reminder that in order to earn

00:44:52.890 --> 00:44:56.640
happiness in later life,
today they need to atone for past sins.

00:44:59.820 --> 00:45:02.190
Master liked this panel,

00:45:02.190 --> 00:45:05.160
I am also very proud of it but...

00:45:12.040 --> 00:45:15.050
So this time it happened in broad daylight.

00:45:56.710 --> 00:46:00.600
The season of white magnolia has come to an end...

00:46:10.900 --> 00:46:14.140
That... Maybe
it's dementia?

00:46:14.140 --> 00:46:16.780
That panel with hell, it's probably
just too realistic...

00:46:16.780 --> 00:46:18.940
But that's not all there's to it.

00:46:18.940 --> 00:46:23.740
Once the Madam felt bad
and remained bedridden,

00:46:23.740 --> 00:46:27.630
the Master certainly knew,
the panel could be the cause

00:46:27.630 --> 00:46:30.440
but refused to part with it.

00:46:30.940 --> 00:46:32.810
After that...

00:47:32.920 --> 00:47:33.920
Dear!

00:47:43.040 --> 00:47:45.200
Fortunately, the fire was quickly overcome,

00:47:45.200 --> 00:47:48.090
but the disease has become even harder on the Madam.

00:47:48.700 --> 00:47:52.160
So I was asked me to find out if it's possible to do anything about it.

00:47:53.050 --> 00:47:56.270
You sure drew something dangerous, Oei-chan.

00:47:58.540 --> 00:48:01.900
It seems that an excess of talent
can also be a problem.

00:48:01.900 --> 00:48:02.650
Heh!

00:48:02.650 --> 00:48:06.220
This means that Oei lacks experience.

00:48:06.220 --> 00:48:09.290
Let me look at the sketches.

00:48:16.720 --> 00:48:19.290
It's as I thought...

00:48:19.290 --> 00:48:22.500
Each time you draw,
you never bring work to the end.

00:48:22.500 --> 00:48:24.890
This painting is not complete.

00:48:24.890 --> 00:48:26.300
Not completed?

00:48:27.360 --> 00:48:30.410
Oei, take me to the house.

00:48:30.410 --> 00:48:33.040
No no!
It's night now too.

00:48:33.040 --> 00:48:37.500
Hey, Manjidou, next time you won't get away with just a small fire.

00:49:37.320 --> 00:49:38.890
Put it up.

00:49:43.870 --> 00:49:45.130
Look...

00:49:54.460 --> 00:49:55.680
See?

00:49:55.680 --> 00:49:58.670
Now the painting is complete.

00:50:06.050 --> 00:50:09.210
Sir, now you'll be fine.

00:50:09.950 --> 00:50:11.340
I'm in your debt.

00:50:17.100 --> 00:50:19.610
You still have much to learn.

00:50:30.120 --> 00:50:32.910
Sensei! Sensei...

00:50:34.910 --> 00:50:36.180
Look!

00:50:45.020 --> 00:50:49.630
<i> Since then, the Madam stopped being afraid of the painting.</i>

00:50:50.420 --> 00:50:51.810
<i> Damn that Tetsuzo!</i>

00:50:51.810 --> 00:50:54.940
<i> It's humiliating, but he's still
one or two steps ahead of me.</i>

00:51:06.820 --> 00:51:08.180
I will redraw it.

00:51:08.180 --> 00:51:10.630
Please explain what I failed.

00:51:10.630 --> 00:51:12.830
I didn't say that the painting hasn't good.

00:51:12.830 --> 00:51:15.790
But if I had to keep it short...

00:51:15.790 --> 00:51:20.260
You are too serious, Oei-san.
That is the problem.

00:51:20.260 --> 00:51:23.020
Every artist has
its strengths and weaknesses.

00:51:23.020 --> 00:51:24.940
Zen-san is a good example of this.

00:51:24.940 --> 00:51:28.360
His erotic paintings released this spring sold very well.

00:51:28.360 --> 00:51:32.020
From the viewpoint of painting techniques,
his are still far from yours.

00:51:32.020 --> 00:51:34.300
All his characters have large heads and skinny little hands,

00:51:34.300 --> 00:51:36.720
but these strange proportions are his main weapon.

00:51:36.720 --> 00:51:41.140
They give his paintings
a special appeal.

00:51:41.480 --> 00:51:44.940
It is obvious that in this lies its strength.

00:51:45.530 --> 00:51:47.480
And with you, Oei-san, it's just the opposite.

00:51:47.480 --> 00:51:50.450
Your portraits are of technical mastery, but they lack any sensuality.

00:51:51.360 --> 00:51:54.080
But it's not your fault.

00:51:54.080 --> 00:51:59.740
Hokusai-sensei, is to blame for making his daughter draw such paintings.

00:52:06.000 --> 00:52:07.340
Hatsugoro-san?

00:52:07.340 --> 00:52:08.510
Where are you headed?

00:52:08.510 --> 00:52:11.260
I was at Manjidou's, and am now going home.

00:52:11.870 --> 00:52:14.320
And I had a meeting at Suhara-ya.

00:52:14.320 --> 00:52:15.720
I'll take you home.

00:52:15.720 --> 00:52:17.460
Isn't that a bother?

00:52:17.460 --> 00:52:21.340
No. I have long wanted
to meet with Hokusai-sensei.

00:52:34.280 --> 00:52:36.890
You will get wet like that.

00:52:44.490 --> 00:52:45.740
<i> What's this smell?</i>

00:52:47.360 --> 00:52:48.560
<i> Hair oil?</i>

00:52:51.020 --> 00:52:55.200
The owner of Suhara-ya told me
he wanted to meet with Zen-san.

00:52:55.200 --> 00:52:56.370
With Zenjirou?

00:52:57.580 --> 00:52:58.850
With that excuse for a man?

00:52:59.780 --> 00:53:02.520
But his paintings of women
are very interesting.

00:53:02.520 --> 00:53:04.160
They are different from the rest.

00:53:05.820 --> 00:53:06.790
Erotic?

00:53:07.290 --> 00:53:08.220
Perhaps...

00:53:09.450 --> 00:53:11.790
He draws great women.

00:53:20.830 --> 00:53:23.920
I... I hate those vulgar paintings!

00:53:33.160 --> 00:53:34.990
I remembered I had something else to do.

00:53:34.990 --> 00:53:36.100
Excuse me...

00:53:42.050 --> 00:53:43.430
<i> It was the smell of skin.</i>

00:53:44.440 --> 00:53:46.740
<i> Not like Tetsuzo or Zenjirou.</i>

00:53:47.440 --> 00:53:48.500
<i> The skin...</i>

00:53:54.830 --> 00:53:56.000
Welcome.

00:53:56.630 --> 00:53:58.630
Do you have a favorite?

00:53:59.020 --> 00:54:00.570
Doesn't matter...

00:54:00.870 --> 00:54:01.920
How was it?

00:54:01.920 --> 00:54:03.060
Be sure to come again!

00:54:03.060 --> 00:54:04.730
I got it, I got it.

00:54:05.620 --> 00:54:07.530
Come on, let me go.

00:54:08.720 --> 00:54:09.740
See you.

00:54:09.740 --> 00:54:11.970
I'll be wait.
– We look forward to your next visit.

00:54:13.010 --> 00:54:14.330
Is this your first time?

00:54:14.330 --> 00:54:16.550
Would you like to take a look and choose then?

00:54:22.350 --> 00:54:25.130
Don't ever come back!

00:54:25.470 --> 00:54:27.100
Ouch...

00:54:29.340 --> 00:54:31.130
Hey!
What's wrong?

00:54:31.780 --> 00:54:34.040
This is stupid so I'm going home.
Let me go!

00:54:34.040 --> 00:54:36.850
The stupid things are the most fun!

00:54:36.850 --> 00:54:37.550
Let's go!

00:54:38.270 --> 00:54:39.470
Let me go, you fool!

00:54:39.470 --> 00:54:41.390
Yes, yes, I'm a happy fool.

00:54:41.800 --> 00:54:44.720
Then, manager,
I'm not taking anymore visitors today!

00:54:44.720 --> 00:54:45.930
Hey...

00:54:50.780 --> 00:54:51.680
Take off your clothes.

00:54:51.680 --> 00:54:52.490
What?!

00:54:53.800 --> 00:54:56.140
Your clothes are all wet...

00:54:56.590 --> 00:54:58.110
You're gonna ruin the tatami.

00:54:58.800 --> 00:55:00.560
Here. You can wear this.

00:55:11.740 --> 00:55:12.760
A furisode?

00:55:13.180 --> 00:55:15.830
My name Kichiya. Pleased to meet you.

00:55:19.220 --> 00:55:20.780
Then, let's start, let's start!

00:55:42.270 --> 00:55:43.450
You know...

00:56:01.690 --> 00:56:03.240
The painting is called "Yamagoshi Amida."

00:56:03.240 --> 00:56:04.740
I think it's made by Kano Tanyu...

00:56:04.740 --> 00:56:05.420
Idiot.

00:56:05.420 --> 00:56:07.770
Tanyu wouldn't never scribble something like this.

00:56:08.400 --> 00:56:09.290
Is it bad?

00:56:09.810 --> 00:56:10.960
Awful.

00:56:11.690 --> 00:56:12.450
Hmm...

00:56:12.740 --> 00:56:14.240
You seem to understand this.

00:56:14.240 --> 00:56:17.810
And why is such a religious painting here?

00:56:18.420 --> 00:56:21.170
Some bothersome monks come here often,

00:56:21.170 --> 00:56:23.240
so I thought this would protect me.

00:56:24.720 --> 00:56:26.480
But it doesn't help...

00:56:27.080 --> 00:56:30.770
The monks that come here,
they aren't afraid of the gods or Buddha.

00:56:32.160 --> 00:56:33.220
I figure.

00:56:35.470 --> 00:56:38.470
By the way, I recently had a
a strange dream.

00:56:39.440 --> 00:56:40.730
Almost like this painting.

00:56:41.120 --> 00:56:43.920
From the mountain, Buddha suddenly appeared.

00:56:44.890 --> 00:56:48.560
Everyone just started to bow down and shout: "Thank you! Thank you!"

00:56:54.250 --> 00:56:57.090
And then He just crushed them all together with houses

00:56:57.090 --> 00:56:59.080
and continued on his way without looking back.

00:57:01.410 --> 00:57:04.140
Terrible, right?

00:57:12.400 --> 00:57:14.460
I wonder if heaven exists at all?

00:57:18.380 --> 00:57:20.600
Well?
Wanna stop this?

00:57:31.320 --> 00:57:33.200
Excellent! Let's do it!

00:58:22.910 --> 00:58:23.870
Hey.

00:58:24.810 --> 00:58:26.230
I'm sorry.

00:58:26.230 --> 00:58:27.960
Let me sleep a little bit.

00:58:27.960 --> 00:58:31.000
Count to a hundred and wake me up.

00:58:31.390 --> 00:58:32.330
I promise.

00:58:33.280 --> 00:58:35.790
Don't forget...

00:58:40.290 --> 00:58:41.320
TL: Oei says 'omoi' which can be translated both as 'heavy' and 'feelings' (emotions).

00:58:40.290 --> 00:58:41.320
<i> Heavy...</i>

00:59:26.470 --> 00:59:28.250
<i> Does heaven exist?</i>

00:59:29.570 --> 00:59:30.800
<i> And hell?</i>

00:59:56.420 --> 00:59:57.730
Well, everything is ready.

00:59:57.730 --> 00:59:59.620
Thank you very much!

01:00:01.950 --> 01:00:03.470
By the way...

01:00:06.440 --> 01:00:09.730
Oei-san, Danjuro is giving a performance tonight. What do you say?

01:00:09.730 --> 01:00:10.760
The play will be Sukeroku.

01:00:10.760 --> 01:00:12.710
[Nakamura Theater]

01:00:13.060 --> 01:00:15.240
I was meant to go with my assistant,

01:00:15.240 --> 01:00:17.300
but something came up.

01:00:17.300 --> 01:00:19.060
Only one seat left though.

01:00:19.060 --> 01:00:20.030
Well...

01:00:20.800 --> 01:00:23.150
Go, you won't regret it.
You'll learn a lot.

01:00:23.590 --> 01:00:24.610
Thank you.

01:00:24.930 --> 01:00:25.940
Then...

01:00:28.180 --> 01:00:30.400
Hatsugoro-san should also be there.

01:00:30.400 --> 01:00:32.620
I gave him the other one.

01:00:40.420 --> 01:00:41.250
Excuse me...

01:00:42.090 --> 01:00:43.180
Oei-san!

01:00:43.760 --> 01:00:45.340
Oei-san, is that you?

01:00:45.820 --> 01:00:46.590
Yeah.

01:00:49.020 --> 01:00:52.400
Something wrong?
You look lost in thought.

01:00:52.870 --> 01:00:54.350
No, nothing special.

01:00:54.850 --> 01:00:56.140
Where you are going?

01:00:56.140 --> 01:00:58.320
Just back home.

01:00:58.320 --> 01:00:59.840
What a coincidence!

01:00:59.840 --> 01:01:02.590
I'm also returning home from the printer.

01:01:05.560 --> 01:01:07.700
By the way, today is the festival of the 46,000 days.

01:01:07.700 --> 01:01:10.020
Would you like to go honor
Kannon-sama with me?

01:01:26.330 --> 01:01:30.990
Personally, I don't like intrusive
or too whiny women.

01:01:30.990 --> 01:01:33.380
I like the composed girls,

01:01:33.380 --> 01:01:36.360
that can defend and assert themselves

01:01:41.330 --> 01:01:43.320
As soon as I saw you for the first time,

01:01:43.320 --> 01:01:48.250
I immediately thought:
"Oh! That's it! She's very, very special."

01:01:49.520 --> 01:01:51.820
I mean...

01:01:54.540 --> 01:01:56.920
I want to tell you how I...

01:02:01.360 --> 01:02:02.990
Thank you for your business!

01:02:02.990 --> 01:02:03.780
Yeah.

01:02:11.440 --> 01:02:13.400
What did you wish for?

01:02:13.400 --> 01:02:14.410
An easy birth.

01:02:14.410 --> 01:02:15.520
Uh?!

01:02:15.520 --> 01:02:16.430
I'm joking.

01:02:16.850 --> 01:02:20.190
Don't tease me, Oei-san.

01:02:26.300 --> 01:02:27.560
What time is it now?

01:02:27.560 --> 01:02:30.650
Well...
It was noon just now

01:02:30.650 --> 01:02:33.160
so maybe two now?

01:02:34.810 --> 01:02:36.220
Do you have something to do?

01:02:36.730 --> 01:02:38.660
No, not really.

01:02:40.520 --> 01:02:42.580
How does tokoroten sound?

01:02:42.580 --> 01:02:43.550
Sure.

01:02:43.550 --> 01:02:44.840
Alright!

01:02:45.830 --> 01:02:47.820
Two tokoroten please!

01:02:47.820 --> 01:02:48.850
Coming up!

01:02:49.950 --> 01:02:51.820
Sorry! I think I'll go.

01:02:52.090 --> 01:02:53.520
Eh?!

01:02:54.060 --> 01:02:55.260
Oei-san!

01:03:31.690 --> 01:03:32.730
What's wrong with her?

01:04:09.840 --> 01:04:11.820
Mom, it's delicious!

01:04:11.820 --> 01:04:15.230
Did you like it?
You can eat mother's too.

01:04:15.230 --> 01:04:16.880
Really?!

01:04:16.880 --> 01:04:18.240
I won't give it back.

01:04:18.240 --> 01:04:19.630
I think I'll eat it after all.

01:04:19.630 --> 01:04:20.460
No!

01:04:26.840 --> 01:04:29.530
It seems that Onao isn't feeling very well.

01:04:34.290 --> 01:04:36.570
I was just at mother's place

01:04:36.570 --> 01:04:38.090
and Onao was in bed...

01:04:38.090 --> 01:04:39.960
The day before yesterday she had a fever too,

01:04:39.960 --> 01:04:42.000
but it wasn't anything serious.

01:04:42.000 --> 01:04:44.300
Mom says she'll get better soon.

01:04:49.000 --> 01:04:51.050
Why don't you go see her?

01:04:51.050 --> 01:04:53.070
Onao will be happy.

01:04:53.440 --> 01:04:54.350
Yeah.

01:04:57.990 --> 01:05:00.220
Are you so afraid of getting sick?!

01:05:00.220 --> 01:05:01.920
You sit around all day doing nothing,

01:05:01.920 --> 01:05:04.130
but to go see Onao
for some reason, you never can!

01:06:02.220 --> 01:06:05.180
Birds! Birds!

01:06:05.180 --> 01:06:07.130
Captured birds!

01:06:07.970 --> 01:06:11.350
Good people,
please free these poor sparrows!

01:06:12.000 --> 01:06:16.510
Captured birds! The unfortunate birds!

01:06:18.870 --> 01:06:20.990
How many birds are in your cells?

01:06:21.580 --> 01:06:24.490
About 30.

01:06:25.360 --> 01:06:27.680
Take it and release all of them.

01:06:27.680 --> 01:06:30.250
Right, thank you very much.

01:06:39.260 --> 01:06:40.120
Hello.

01:06:40.650 --> 01:06:41.550
Oh!

01:06:43.360 --> 01:06:45.960
You became very superstitious.

01:06:45.960 --> 01:06:49.660
But something like that,
it won't really help.

01:06:49.660 --> 01:06:52.360
All these birds are clipped feathers,

01:06:52.360 --> 01:06:54.720
so they'll quickly be caught back.

01:06:54.720 --> 01:06:56.220
Really?

01:06:56.220 --> 01:07:01.360
Nevertheless, there will always be a few
lucky ones who manage to escape.

01:07:02.630 --> 01:07:04.830
Then, are you coming home?

01:07:05.550 --> 01:07:07.260
Onao will be happy.

01:07:07.260 --> 01:07:09.680
And I made rice sweets!

01:07:09.680 --> 01:07:11.120
That's rare...

01:07:11.120 --> 01:07:13.340
We can eat them together.

01:07:59.930 --> 01:08:01.740
Only sweets...

01:08:05.690 --> 01:08:07.180
Is she sleeping?

01:08:07.180 --> 01:08:08.740
Just fell asleep.

01:08:21.320 --> 01:08:22.320
Who's there?

01:08:23.740 --> 01:08:26.440
Onao, how do you feel?

01:08:28.380 --> 01:08:30.120
It's dad!

01:08:49.120 --> 01:08:53.020
<i> Death is the most feared thing on Earth.</i>

01:08:53.020 --> 01:08:55.720
<i> I will erase it and never die.</i>

01:09:00.750 --> 01:09:03.010
<i> I will erase it...</i>

01:09:09.630 --> 01:09:12.350
Oei, could you take this painting

01:09:12.350 --> 01:09:14.500
to your mother's place tomorrow?

01:09:15.040 --> 01:09:16.010
Yeah...

01:09:16.730 --> 01:09:18.820
Tell them that it drives away evil.

01:09:36.860 --> 01:09:39.320
The general is as stiff as a brush, has a beard,

01:09:39.320 --> 01:09:40.710
and in his hand is a sword.

01:09:43.210 --> 01:09:46.980
With his long sword,
he can easily cut any illness.

01:09:47.950 --> 01:09:52.080
And with his other hand,
he strangles any pain.

01:09:52.600 --> 01:09:54.880
He looks very scary,

01:09:54.880 --> 01:09:57.150
but he's actually a spirit that protects children.

01:09:57.150 --> 01:10:00.040
Does dad hate me?

01:10:00.040 --> 01:10:01.080
Why?

01:10:01.080 --> 01:10:05.100
Dad doesn't like sick people...

01:10:05.100 --> 01:10:08.940
Tetsuzo is a coward,
he's just scared of getting sick.

01:10:09.860 --> 01:10:11.400
But you are different.

01:10:11.400 --> 01:10:14.010
That's why he painted this painting for you.

01:10:26.750 --> 01:10:28.960
Your hands are really soft.

01:10:34.620 --> 01:10:36.640
Now that you're back home,

01:10:36.640 --> 01:10:40.200
let's stop cutting your hair
and let it grow longer.

01:10:40.200 --> 01:10:42.480
I'll do your hair.

01:10:42.480 --> 01:10:43.770
Really?

01:10:43.770 --> 01:10:44.560
Yeah.

01:10:45.310 --> 01:10:47.390
She's very good at it.

01:10:47.390 --> 01:10:49.520
Her hair always looks great.

01:10:49.520 --> 01:10:51.690
I see. So you're good?

01:10:51.690 --> 01:10:53.320
Look forward to it.

01:10:53.320 --> 01:10:55.280
I hope that your hair grows back quickly.

01:10:59.180 --> 01:11:01.260
Can I stay the night here?

01:11:01.260 --> 01:11:03.390
Ah, that's a good idea.

01:11:03.390 --> 01:11:05.960
Let's all sleep together tonight.

01:11:32.270 --> 01:11:33.200
Nee...

01:11:34.190 --> 01:11:35.620
Nee-chan, are you asleep?

01:11:36.290 --> 01:11:37.340
I'm awake.

01:11:37.860 --> 01:11:40.280
There's something on the net.

01:11:40.280 --> 01:11:41.100
What?

01:11:48.920 --> 01:11:50.160
Just sitting there.

01:12:25.470 --> 01:12:27.240
It's just a big bug.

01:12:30.200 --> 01:12:32.990
I chased it out,
so don't be afraid.

01:12:34.870 --> 01:12:35.800
Bug?

01:12:37.040 --> 01:12:38.410
A beautiful bug?

01:12:38.410 --> 01:12:39.480
Yes.

01:12:39.480 --> 01:12:43.930
With long, thin legs,
and a bright shell.

01:12:55.270 --> 01:12:56.640
Friendly?

01:12:56.640 --> 01:12:58.080
Really friendly.

01:12:58.600 --> 01:12:59.820
Cute?

01:12:59.820 --> 01:13:01.050
Really cute.

01:13:09.640 --> 01:13:10.860
Nee...

01:13:12.550 --> 01:13:15.520
When I die, I'm going to hell.

01:13:19.230 --> 01:13:24.130
And in hell, my job will be
carry stones to Ojizou-sama.

01:13:24.130 --> 01:13:25.100
Why?

01:13:25.100 --> 01:13:26.380
What do you mean "why"?

01:13:26.380 --> 01:13:28.860
Because that's how it is.
There's nothing you can do about it.

01:13:54.490 --> 01:13:56.360
Do you want something?

01:14:08.650 --> 01:14:10.990
She has been looking better recently.

01:14:14.540 --> 01:14:15.790
Yeah.

01:14:26.920 --> 01:14:31.660
It's fine. It's nothing serious, she'll get better soon.

01:14:33.450 --> 01:14:34.780
You know...

01:14:36.250 --> 01:14:38.780
Bring your father with you next time.

01:14:41.030 --> 01:14:43.480
Tetsuzo is a really big crybaby...

01:14:45.680 --> 01:14:47.130
Silly...

01:14:47.130 --> 01:14:49.520
I'm also a crybaby.

01:14:59.900 --> 01:15:02.830
The medicine has been working.
She has been feeling much better.

01:15:03.530 --> 01:15:05.770
Last night she even ate porridge.

01:15:05.770 --> 01:15:07.740
Come visit her today.

01:15:08.630 --> 01:15:10.810
You still haven't learned to lie.

01:15:10.810 --> 01:15:13.260
That's why you haven't caught a man yet.

01:15:27.420 --> 01:15:28.860
This is strange...

01:15:29.440 --> 01:15:32.650
It felt like I was being followed by a little girl...

01:15:37.610 --> 01:15:41.310
This girl... How did she look?

01:15:41.950 --> 01:15:44.830
Well, all old-fashioned...

01:15:44.830 --> 01:15:46.280
Short haired.

01:16:14.990 --> 01:16:18.330
Wow!
What a strong wind.

01:17:06.760 --> 01:17:10.240
You managed to come by yourself.

01:18:08.600 --> 01:18:10.480
She left.

01:18:38.030 --> 01:18:43.260
Maybe it was I who stole her vision and life...

01:18:43.990 --> 01:18:45.110
Eh?

01:19:38.180 --> 01:19:39.190
This is strange...

01:19:43.740 --> 01:19:46.990
It wasn't a joke!

01:19:46.990 --> 01:19:50.080
I really felt like someone was following me!

01:19:50.080 --> 01:19:52.240
It's true!

01:19:52.240 --> 01:19:53.600
Dumb Zen,

01:19:53.600 --> 01:19:56.620
behind you, there's someone there.

01:19:57.050 --> 01:19:58.010
What?

01:20:05.930 --> 01:20:07.520
Excuse me brother.

01:20:07.520 --> 01:20:11.120
Ku-Kuninao!
So it was you, the one creeping?!

01:20:11.120 --> 01:20:12.940
I was walking behind you the entire time,

01:20:12.940 --> 01:20:14.940
but you never seemed to notice.

01:20:17.450 --> 01:20:19.610
Sensei, Oei-san.

01:20:20.080 --> 01:20:21.960
Glad to see you in good health.

01:20:22.430 --> 01:20:23.400
Yeah.

01:20:23.740 --> 01:20:25.200
And you too.

01:20:27.790 --> 01:20:29.100
You too, brother.

01:20:29.100 --> 01:20:30.480
Shut up!

01:20:30.480 --> 01:20:32.920
What the hell are you doing here?!

01:20:32.920 --> 01:20:37.180
What? An interesting woman appeared in Fukagawa.

01:20:37.180 --> 01:20:40.360
They say she can drink
an awful lot.

01:20:40.360 --> 01:20:42.480
Even more than you?

01:20:42.480 --> 01:20:43.730
Who knows...

01:20:43.730 --> 01:20:48.110
That's why I would like to
take part in a contest with her.

01:20:48.110 --> 01:20:50.150
And there's a prize?

01:20:50.150 --> 01:20:50.780
Yeah.

01:20:50.780 --> 01:20:54.360
They say that the winner will be allowed to see a rare tattoo on her back.

01:20:54.360 --> 01:20:57.160
Apparently no one ever saw it before!

01:20:57.870 --> 01:21:00.110
Hmm! Waste of time.

01:21:12.010 --> 01:21:14.090
I will go eat noodles or something...

01:21:16.270 --> 01:21:19.870
Excellent! I'm with you!

01:21:19.870 --> 01:21:21.320
Oei-san, see you!

01:21:21.320 --> 01:21:22.920
Come on, come on!

01:21:23.590 --> 01:21:25.920
Manjidou might come,

01:21:25.920 --> 01:21:28.510
we'll lose face if we don't finish in time.

01:21:28.510 --> 01:21:31.720
That face is nothing to worry about.

01:21:31.720 --> 01:21:35.050
I leave the drawing to you.
I'm counting on you.

01:21:35.410 --> 01:21:37.290
I won't draw it!

01:21:38.030 --> 01:21:41.660
Oei! I just remembered:
Manjidou was saying

01:21:41.660 --> 01:21:45.740
that it should be time for you to start drawing under your own name.

01:21:54.480 --> 01:21:58.700
It seems like the night today will be a long one... Right?

01:23:10.730 --> 01:23:13.600
<i> Onao, how are you doing?</i>

01:23:14.620 --> 01:23:19.790
<i> I know for sure that you didn't go to hell.</i>

01:23:20.970 --> 01:23:22.910
<i> We're still doing the same here.</i>

01:23:22.910 --> 01:23:25.640
<i> Not particularly good nor bad,</i>

01:23:25.640 --> 01:23:27.720
<i> but we're still happy.</i>

01:23:29.400 --> 01:23:30.680
Right?

01:24:19.450 --> 01:24:21.530
<i> Tetsuzo never stopped painting</i>

01:24:21.530 --> 01:24:23.360
<i> and lived to be ninety years old.</i>

01:24:24.810 --> 01:24:28.090
<i> Zenjirou took the name Keisai Eisen</i>

01:24:28.090 --> 01:24:30.810
<i> and even became a bit famous with his bijin-ga.</i>

01:24:30.810 --> 01:24:33.450
<i> He died a year before Tetsuzo.</i>

01:24:34.190 --> 01:24:36.280
<i> That dumb Zen...</i>

01:24:38.040 --> 01:24:39.900
<i> I married once,</i>

01:24:39.900 --> 01:24:42.220
<i> but we parted ways and I returned home to Tetsuzo.</i>

01:24:42.220 --> 01:24:44.830
<i> Ended up living with him until he died.</i>

01:24:45.450 --> 01:24:48.350
<i> Tetsuzo planned to live more than a hundred years,</i>

01:24:48.350 --> 01:24:50.680
<i> but ended up only lasting ninety.</i>

01:24:51.470 --> 01:24:54.700
<i> Even at death's door, he wanted ten more...</i>

01:24:54.700 --> 01:25:00.960
<i> "Just another five years, all I needed to become a real artist," is what he said.</i>

01:25:00.960 --> 01:25:02.490
<i> And he was serious.</i>

01:25:03.070 --> 01:25:05.210
<i> What an unbelievable old man...</i>

01:25:15.060 --> 01:25:30.310
After the death of Hokusai, Oei moved many times, and died in the year 4 AD Ansei (1857), 9 years after her father's death.
Nobody knows where she was buried.

01:25:35.320 --> 01:25:52.000
11 years after the death of Oei, with the fall of the Tokugawa shogunate, the era of the samurai swiftly ended. The new government of Meiji renamed the city of Edo to Tokyo.
